1
00:00:00,214 --> 00:00:01,604
اَعُوْذُ بِاللهِ مِنَّ الشِّيْطَانِ الرَّجِيْمِ۝

2
00:00:02,738 --> 00:00:03,808
بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمَانِ الرَّحِيْمَ۝

3
00:00:03,866 --> 00:00:08,524
  اَلْحَمْدُ لله وَالصَّلَاةُ وَالسَّلَامُ عَلى سَيِّدِنَا محمد وَعَلَى اَلِهِ وَصَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ

4
00:00:11,152 --> 00:00:12,702
14, Zaat-Ur-Riqa(ذات الرقاع),

5
00:00:14,101 --> 00:00:17,754
it occurred in Jamada Al-Oula(جمادى ألأولى) Fourth of Hijrah(هجرة).

6
00:00:18,512 --> 00:00:22,227
 It was named Zaat-Ur-Riqa(ذات الرقاع), which means the Battle of the rags.

7
00:00:23,073 --> 00:00:25,781
Why it was called that, why it was given that name?

8
00:00:25,819 --> 00:00:30,220
Because because the shoes of the Muslims were tearing apart

9
00:00:30,272 --> 00:00:34,828
and their feet were bleeding so they ended up wrapping pieces of their clothes over their feet.

10
00:00:35,958 --> 00:00:39,142
 Rasool Allah ﷺ attacked the land of Najd(نجد) but no fighting occurred.

11
00:00:39,689 --> 00:00:45,115
15, the minor battle of Badr(بدر) it happened in Sha'ban(شعبان) year four.

12
00:00:45,678 --> 00:00:49,818
Rasool Allah ﷺ went to Badr(بدر) to meet Abu Sufiyan(أبوسُفيان) and Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) at an appointed time.

13
00:00:50,484 --> 00:00:52,421
 He went with 1500 fighters.

14
00:00:52,779 --> 00:00:55,863
 Abu Sufiyan(أبوسُفيان) made it halfway but then decided to go back to Makkah.

15
00:00:58,119 --> 00:00:59,636
Number 16, Domat-Ul-Jandal(دومة الجندل),

16
00:01:00,824 --> 00:01:05,253
Domat-Ul-Jandal(دومة الجندل), is at the extreme southern tip of Ash-Sham(ألشَّام).

17
00:01:06,377 --> 00:01:10,593
Domat-Ul-Jandal(دومة الجندل), is the borders between the Arabian Peninsula and Ash-Sham(ألشَّام).

18
00:01:11,377 --> 00:01:14,934
 It is a town surrounded by an impregnable wall.

19
00:01:16,266 --> 00:01:21,371
Rasool Allah ﷺ attacked it, when he heard that the non believers are gathering an army to invade Madina.

20
00:01:22,699 --> 00:01:25,889
So Rasool Allah ﷺ would not wait for an enemy to come to him, he would go out and meet them.

21
00:01:26,266 --> 00:01:30,413
He heard that they're mobilizing an army he went out all the way to Ash-Sham(ألشَّام).

22
00:01:31,429 --> 00:01:33,780
He marched towards them, in an army of 1000,

23
00:01:34,381 --> 00:01:36,516
he would move at night and hide during the day.

24
00:01:37,175 --> 00:01:38,835
When the enemy heard of his move.

25
00:01:38,911 --> 00:01:41,147
They feared him and ended up dispersing.

26
00:01:41,872 --> 00:01:45,972
So when Rasool Allah ﷺ arrived in their territory, none of them came out to fight.

27
00:01:46,985 --> 00:01:50,183
He attacked their shepherds and confiscated some of their cattle

28
00:01:50,679 --> 00:01:53,524
 and sent out detachments to different areas and then returned.

29
00:01:54,501 --> 00:01:55,809
Number 17, Al-Khandaq(ألخندق),

30
00:01:56,381 --> 00:02:00,576
the Battle of the Trench occurred in Shawal(شوال), fifth of Hijrah(هجرة).

31
00:02:01,322 --> 00:02:03,624
Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) came headed by Abu Sufiyan(أبوسُفيان),

32
00:02:04,346 --> 00:02:06,829
Banu Fuzara(بنوفزارة) were headed by Oyena Bin Hasan(عيينة بن حصن),

33
00:02:07,585 --> 00:02:09,730
Bano Murrah(بنومرَّة) headed by Haris Bin Aof(حارث بن عوف),

34
00:02:10,222 --> 00:02:12,352
In addition to Ghatafan(غطافان) and Ash'jah(أشجاع),

35
00:02:12,784 --> 00:02:16,292
and they all converged on Madina in an army of 5000.

36
00:02:19,416 --> 00:02:20,032
Allah O Alam(ألله أعلم),

37
00:02:20,089 --> 00:02:24,165
this number is underestimate, should be more than 5000.

38
00:02:25,085 --> 00:02:27,864
When Rasool Allah ﷺ receive news of the armies.

39
00:02:28,382 --> 00:02:29,838
 He consulted with the Sahabah(صحابه),

40
00:02:30,371 --> 00:02:37,135
and that is one Salman Farsi(سلمان فارسي) suggested digging the trench, which was a novel idea to Arab warfare.

41
00:02:37,974 --> 00:02:42,895
The trench was completed with a little over 10 days, the Muslims were 3000.

42
00:02:44,108 --> 00:02:47,704
So this was a coalition that attacked Madina.

43
00:02:48,706 --> 00:02:56,411
It was made up of Quraish(قريش), Ghatafan(غطافان), Ash'jah(أشجاع) some other tribes,

44
00:02:56,727 --> 00:02:59,498
alongside, Al-Munafiqoon(ألمنافقون) from within Madina.

45
00:03:00,125 --> 00:03:02,427
And later on, Banu Quraidha(بنوقريظه).

46
00:03:04,069 --> 00:03:10,964
Rasool Allah ﷺ heard the news of this advance, and the army was large, the army of the Kuffar(كفار).

47
00:03:13,042 --> 00:03:15,720
So, Salman Farsi(سلمان فارسي) suggested this idea, he said:

48
00:03:15,801 --> 00:03:19,111
This is something that we do in Persia, so this was an imported idea.

49
00:03:20,122 --> 00:03:23,034
This was an idea that was not known to the Arabs.

50
00:03:24,104 --> 00:03:25,975
Salman Farsi(سلمان فارسي) said: Let's dig a trench.

51
00:03:26,945 --> 00:03:30,173
The Trench was dug, north of Madina.

52
00:03:31,382 --> 00:03:35,660
Even though Makkah is towards the south, Why was it to the north of Madina.?

53
00:03:38,847 --> 00:03:42,368
Because Madina had natural defenses from the three other sides,

54
00:03:42,854 --> 00:03:50,468
 from the eastern and the west it was defended by a volcanic rocky track, very sharp rocks.

55
00:03:51,306 --> 00:03:53,650
It's very difficult for an army to march through,

56
00:03:54,118 --> 00:03:56,495
and then you have the palm groves, towards the south,

57
00:03:57,437 --> 00:04:01,147
 which also makes it very difficult for a large army.

58
00:04:01,752 --> 00:04:07,014
So the trench was built, was dug towards the north of Madina,

59
00:04:07,938 --> 00:04:09,438
an interesting event occurred,

60
00:04:10,510 --> 00:04:15,685
the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم came across this boulder that refused to move out of their way.

61
00:04:16,461 --> 00:04:19,419
They tried to break it, but it would end up breaking their axes.

62
00:04:20,125 --> 00:04:22,427
So they went to Rasool Allah ﷺ and they complained to him.

63
00:04:23,274 --> 00:04:26,934
 Rasool Allah ﷺ went there he asked for an axe they give it to him he said:

64
00:04:27,014 --> 00:04:31,522
 Allah o Akbar(ألله أكبر) and he struck the Boulder,

65
00:04:32,283 --> 00:04:36,090
and it cracked and the spark of light came out of it.

66
00:04:36,205 --> 00:04:37,710
 Rasool Allah ﷺ made Takbir(تكبير).

67
00:04:39,079 --> 00:04:43,848
And then he did it again, it's cracked a second time and light came out,

68
00:04:44,243 --> 00:04:47,481
the third time he hit it, it just broke into pieces.

69
00:04:48,110 --> 00:04:49,304
And Rasool Allah ﷺ made Takbir(تكبير).

70
00:04:49,409 --> 00:04:52,038
Sahabah رضي الله عنهم  said: Why did you make Takbir(تكبير)?

71
00:04:52,751 --> 00:04:58,973
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: Because the first time I saw the palaces of Syria.

72
00:04:59,717 --> 00:05:02,938
  And Allah told me that my Ummah(امة) would enter the land of the Romans.

73
00:05:05,325 --> 00:05:11,642
And I made Takbir(تكبير) the second time because Allah showed me the white palaces of Madaen(مدائن), the capital of Persia,

74
00:05:12,094 --> 00:05:15,152
and Allah told me that my nation will enter the land of Persia,

75
00:05:16,131 --> 00:05:20,306
and the third time I said Allah O Akbar(ألله أكبر) because Allah showed me the gates of San'a(صنعاء) in Yemen,

76
00:05:20,637 --> 00:05:23,067
 and told me that my nation will enter into Yemen.

77
00:05:24,903 --> 00:05:27,501
When was Rasool Allah ﷺ giving this promise,

78
00:05:27,549 --> 00:05:32,085
you've noticed that the greatest promises to this Ummah(امة)

79
00:05:32,400 --> 00:05:36,178
were delivered to the Ummah(امة) when the Ummah(امة) was at its lowest point.

80
00:05:37,883 --> 00:05:40,649
Because these promises were a test of faith,

81
00:05:41,952 --> 00:05:46,852
 Al-Munafiqoon(ألمنافقون) they were laughing so much and mocking at this, they said:

82
00:05:47,582 --> 00:05:50,624
احد على يامن على يخرج لقضاء حاجت

83
00:05:51,446 --> 00:05:55,552
One of us doesn't even feel secure to respond to the call of nature,

84
00:05:56,492 --> 00:06:00,889
and Rasool Allah ﷺ is telling us that we're gonna open Persia and the Roman Empire, and Yemen.

85
00:06:01,835 --> 00:06:02,833
 What is he talking about.?

86
00:06:05,556 --> 00:06:06,619
But the believers said:

87
00:06:06,643 --> 00:06:08,848
هذا ما وعدنا الله ورسوله

88
00:06:09,327 --> 00:06:12,162
Believers say: This is what the Allah and His messenger  promised us, it's gonna happen.

89
00:06:14,461 --> 00:06:18,555
 Another promise that was given by Rasool Allah ﷺ,

90
00:06:19,532 --> 00:06:21,608
another incident to show you when the promises are given,

91
00:06:22,068 --> 00:06:26,701
when Rasool Ullah and Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) are running away from Makkah, they're on the run

92
00:06:28,174 --> 00:06:30,279
 and Quraish(قُرَيْشْ), are pursuing them.

93
00:06:32,102 --> 00:06:37,351
And they place a bounty on the head of Muhammadﷺ One hundred camels.

94
00:06:39,196 --> 00:06:45,648
Suraqah Bin Malik Al-Ashjae(سراقه بن مالك ألأشجاعي) one of the Bedouins, he was sitting among his people he's not from Makkah

95
00:06:45,709 --> 00:06:50,728
 but the news is going around that there's ransom on Muhammadﷺ, Dead or Alive.

96
00:06:52,354 --> 00:06:54,622
 So somebody came in to the gathering and said:

97
00:06:54,647 --> 00:07:01,332
I've seen two men walking in the desert, they might be Muhammadﷺ and his companions.

98
00:07:02,033 --> 00:07:02,628
 Suraqah(سراقه) said:

99
00:07:02,682 --> 00:07:05,840
 No, no, no it's not them. I was there, and I saw them.

100
00:07:07,549 --> 00:07:09,478
But then Suraqah(سراقه) sneaked out of that meeting,

101
00:07:09,938 --> 00:07:17,385
he went to his house, called his horse and ran out in pursuit of the two men,

102
00:07:17,876 --> 00:07:22,676
because he thought these might be Muhammad(محمد) and Abu Bakr(ابوبكر), he wanted 100, camels.

103
00:07:23,614 --> 00:07:24,679
 So, he's pursuing them,

104
00:07:25,197 --> 00:07:28,140
Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) is looking behind, he is looking behind

105
00:07:28,553 --> 00:07:32,918
and Rasool Allah ﷺ is reciting Qur'an, he's not even looking behind

106
00:07:33,586 --> 00:07:37,156
and Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) is very worried, staring behind.

107
00:07:37,296 --> 00:07:40,386
Rasool Allah ﷺ is walking confidently without looking back.

108
00:07:42,628 --> 00:07:46,605
And then Suraqah(سراقه), when he gets close.

109
00:07:48,072 --> 00:07:52,032
The front feet of his horse sink in the sand, and he falls.

110
00:07:53,453 --> 00:07:55,184
He said: My horse never did this.

111
00:07:56,918 --> 00:08:02,379
He jumps on his horse again and pursues Muhammadﷺ, it happens a second time.

112
00:08:04,838 --> 00:08:09,806
And then the third time it happened he saw a wall of dust in front of him.

113
00:08:10,370 --> 00:08:14,516
So he started asking Muhammadﷺ to give him peace.

114
00:08:15,972 --> 00:08:20,396
He's out to capture Muhammadﷺ and he is now asking Muhammadﷺ to give him peace.

115
00:08:21,630 --> 00:08:23,442
 Rasool Allah ﷺ said: I will give you Amaan(أمان),

116
00:08:24,096 --> 00:08:25,515
and then Rasool Allah ﷺ told him:

117
00:08:25,594 --> 00:08:31,972
O Suraqah(سراقه), what about a the day, when you will be wearing the bracelets of Kisra(كسرى).

118
00:08:33,932 --> 00:08:35,385
Now there's only one Kisra(كسرى) in the world.

119
00:08:35,446 --> 00:08:37,844
So, it's very well known who that Kisra(كسرى) is.

120
00:08:38,754 --> 00:08:44,341
But it is such a strange thing to say that Suraqah(سراقه) had to make sure that he heard it right,

121
00:08:44,421 --> 00:08:45,246
he said: Kisra(كسرى)!

122
00:08:45,542 --> 00:08:47,941
 Rasool Allah ﷺ said: Yes Kisra Ibn Hurmz(كسرى إبن هرمز),

123
00:08:48,187 --> 00:08:50,893
Kisra(كسرى) the son of Hurmz(هرمز) to make to make it clear.

124
00:08:52,204 --> 00:08:56,439
Obviously Suraqah(سراقه) didn't understand what that meant, and how would I wear the bracelets of Kisra(كسرى).

125
00:08:56,795 --> 00:08:59,500
Now these bracelets apparently were very famous

126
00:08:59,627 --> 00:09:05,095
it's like something that everybody knew was, special bracelets of Kisra(كسرى).

127
00:09:07,786 --> 00:09:13,744
Suraqah(سراقه) somehow he told Muhammadﷺ to write,

128
00:09:14,736 --> 00:09:16,667
Rasool Allah ﷺ gave him Amaan(أمان), gave him Amaan(أمان), gave him peace.

129
00:09:16,879 --> 00:09:18,582
 Suraqah(سراقه) said: I wanted on paper.

130
00:09:20,011 --> 00:09:22,581
Allah O Alam(ألله أعلم) how came you would ask such a thing.

131
00:09:22,595 --> 00:09:24,206
He said: Write it for me on paper.

132
00:09:24,490 --> 00:09:27,498
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ told Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) write that down for him.

133
00:09:27,763 --> 00:09:31,016
So, Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) wrote down on this sheet of paper.

134
00:09:31,638 --> 00:09:35,588
That Rasool Allah ﷺ is giving Suraqah Bin Malik(سراقه بن مالك) peace.

135
00:09:37,243 --> 00:09:39,581
When the land of Suraqah(سراقه) was opened,

136
00:09:41,255 --> 00:09:44,799
and they were going to kill Suraqah Bin Malik(سراقه بن مالك), few years years later.

137
00:09:45,285 --> 00:09:48,836
Suraqah Bin Malik(سراقه بن مالك) pulls out that paper and says Muhammad(محمد) has given me peace.

138
00:09:49,163 --> 00:09:50,270
And that saves his life.

139
00:09:50,997 --> 00:09:56,074
He then becomes Muslim Rasool Allah ﷺ passes away, Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) passes away Umar(عُمَر) becomes Khalifah(خليفه)

140
00:09:56,385 --> 00:09:58,594
and Suraqah(سراقه) joins the army that's going to persia.

141
00:10:00,906 --> 00:10:08,428
And they conquer Persia, and the treasures of Kisra(كسرى) are brought back to Madina.

142
00:10:09,823 --> 00:10:13,734
And among the treasure, they found the bracelets of Kisra(كسرى).

143
00:10:14,779 --> 00:10:19,915
 Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) called Suraqah(سراقه), to stand up on the pulpit,

144
00:10:21,056 --> 00:10:25,365
and to wear the bracelets of Kisra(كسرى) and to tell the Muslims, the story about it.

145
00:10:26,561 --> 00:10:31,712
Suraqah(سراقه), this simple Bedouin is wearing the bracelets of Kisra Ibn Hurmuz(كسرى إبن هرمز).

146
00:10:32,426 --> 00:10:36,018
But that's a promise that was made by Rasool Allah ﷺ when he was on the run.

147
00:10:37,997 --> 00:10:40,113
 Its takes a lot of faith to believe in something like that.

148
00:10:41,641 --> 00:10:44,423
So now when the Ummah(امة) is at its low point.

149
00:10:46,185 --> 00:10:48,493
And hopefully we have reached the rock bottom,

150
00:10:48,798 --> 00:10:50,385
In Sha Allah(إنْ شاءالله) there's nothing lower than this.

151
00:10:51,034 --> 00:10:53,163
That we can only go up from there.

152
00:10:55,207 --> 00:10:56,890
 Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ has promised this Ummah(امة).

153
00:10:57,176 --> 00:10:58,176
Number one,

154
00:11:00,093 --> 00:11:02,346
تكون فيكم النبوة ما شاء الله أن تكون،

155
00:11:02,948 --> 00:11:04,814
ثم ينزع الله إذاشاء أن ينزعها،

156
00:11:05,556 --> 00:11:12,777
 ثم تكون خلافة راشدة فتكون فيكم ما شاء الله أن تكون ثم ينزع الله إذا شاء أن ينزعها،

157
00:11:14,140 --> 00:11:20,323
ثم تكون ملكًا عاضًا فتكون فيكم ما شاء الله أن تكون ثم ينزعها الله إذا شاء الله أن ينزعها، ،

158
00:11:21,858 --> 00:11:24,484
ثم تكون ملكًا جبرية

159
00:11:24,894 --> 00:11:29,089
فيكون فيكم ما شاء الله أن يكون، ثم ينزعها الله إذا شاء أن ينزعها،

160
00:11:29,337 --> 00:11:32,168
ثم تكون خلافة على منهاج النبوة

161
00:11:32,765 --> 00:11:36,068
Rasool Allah ﷺ says it will first start with prophethood,

162
00:11:37,030 --> 00:11:40,045
 and will stay for as long as Allah wants and then Allah will take it away.

163
00:11:40,826 --> 00:11:45,000
And then it will be Khilafah Rashida(خِلَافَه راشده), rightly guided,

164
00:11:45,445 --> 00:11:49,188
and it will stay among you as long as Allah wants to stayand then Allah will take it away.

165
00:11:50,037 --> 00:11:57,172
And then it will be kingdom, and will stay with you as long as Allah wants to stay and then Allah takes it away,

166
00:11:57,803 --> 00:12:00,807
 and then it will be dictatorship, tyranny.

167
00:12:01,499 --> 00:12:05,311
And it will remain with you as long as Allah wants it to remain and then Allah will take it away.

168
00:12:05,753 --> 00:12:09,053
And then it will be Khilafah(خِلَافَه) on the path of Prophethood.

169
00:12:10,333 --> 00:12:14,493
Right now we're going through that tyrannical dictatorship stage.

170
00:12:15,581 --> 00:12:17,601
 And there's only Khilafah(خِلَافَه) after it.

171
00:12:19,549 --> 00:12:21,398
That's the next stage, it's Khilafah(خِلَافَه).

172
00:12:21,889 --> 00:12:24,870
Number two, Rasool Allah ﷺ says:

173
00:12:25,405 --> 00:12:27,265
إنَّ اللَّهَ زَوَى لي الأرْضَ،

174
00:12:27,576 --> 00:12:30,966
فَرَأَيْتُ (مَشارِقَها ومَغارِبَها)،وإنَّ مُلكَ أُمَّتي سيبلُغُ ما زُوِيَ لي مِنها،

175
00:12:31,839 --> 00:12:36,437
 Rasool Allah ﷺ says: Allah has shrinked the earth in front of my eyes and showed it to me.

176
00:12:37,044 --> 00:12:42,242
 And he told me, that the kingdom of my nation will reach all of it, the entire earth!

177
00:12:43,179 --> 00:12:45,029
Number three Rasool Allah ﷺ says:

178
00:12:45,168 --> 00:12:47,738
سَيَبْلُغن هذا الدين ما بلغ اللَّيل والنَّهار،

179
00:12:47,864 --> 00:12:49,656
 بِعِزِّ عَزِيزٍ أو بِذُلِّ ذَليلٍ، ،

180
00:12:49,992 --> 00:12:53,909
عِزًّا يُعِزُّ الله به الإسلام وذُلًّا يُذِلُّ الله به الشِرك

181
00:12:55,658 --> 00:12:58,317
This religion will reach wherever night and day reaches

182
00:12:58,933 --> 00:13:02,740
every corner of earth, where night and day reaches, this religion will reach.

183
00:13:04,019 --> 00:13:06,370
